/*
   ============================================================
   VAULT OS 0.8
   ESP32-C3 + OLED 128x64 + 4 buttons
   ============================================================

   BUTTONS
   R5 = LEFT  / CHARSET-
   R6 = RIGHT / CHARSET+
   R7 = ENTER / ACCEPT
   R8 = BACK  / DELETE

   PINS
   SDA = GPIO 8
   SCL = GPIO 9
   R5  = GPIO 3
   R6  = GPIO 4
   R7  = GPIO 5
   R8  = GPIO 6

   ============================================================
   CHANGES v0.8
   ============================================================

   UI / UX
   - Locked screen redesigned: shows SSID, AP password,
     IP and a clear hint, so you can connect to the web
     even without the vault being unlocked
   - AP password visible on device (long R5 on Locked)
   - full on-screen keyboard for all text input
     (abc / ABC / 123 / #@!), cursor navigation with 4 buttons
   - keyboard has action row: layout switch, backspace, accept
   - unified editor for all fields: master, name, user,
     password, note, search

   WEB
   - emoji removed
   - Apple-style minimal UI (SF-like typography, soft cards,
     subtle borders, muted palette)
   - consistent spacing, rounded corners, focus rings
   - light/dark aware via prefers-color-scheme
   - reduced CSS, no external assets

   NEW FEATURE: TOTP (2FA) per record
   - each record can hold a Base32 TOTP secret (RFC 6238)
   - 6 digits, 30 s step, HMAC-SHA1
   - code shown on device and in web UI, refreshes live
   - HMAC-SHA1 taken from mbedtls (already linked)

   FIXES
   - web lock no longer freezes the server
   - loop stack pressure reduced (no temp String in draw loop)
   - MAX_RECORDS = 16

   SECURITY (unchanged core)
   - AES-256-CBC + HMAC-SHA256 Encrypt-then-MAC
   - PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 -> 64 bytes
   - MAC verified before decrypt
   - random salt in header, random IV per save
   - atomic writes via .tmp + rename
   - failed password backoff
   - session cookie + CSRF + HTML escaping
   - sensitive RAM wiped where practical
*/

